  "weeklyExtras": {
    "week": 8,
    "tagline": "Week 8 News · Division Races · Playoff Pressure · Full Rankings",
    "kicker": "GFL Insider · Week 8",
    "headline": "THE FAVORITES BLINKED. THE RACE GOT LOUDER.",
    "deck": "California lost its second straight, Sullco seized the East, Medford shocked Simpson Sith, and the Central turned into a four-team pressure chamber. With six regular-season weeks left, every division now has a live chase.",
    "story": [
      "Week 8 did not crown a front-runner. It made the league less comfortable. Redwood Murder improved to 7-1, but did it with 94.24 points, ninth-best on the weekly slate. California Un-Named Team fell to 6-2 after posting 93.48, while Sullco MethMouths used a 101.86-93.48 win to reach 6-2 and take control of the East race.",
      "The Central became the league’s pressure chamber. Turbulent Ticklesh!ts answered its Week 7 collapse with 127.46, the best score of Week 8, and moved to 5-3. Medford MountainMen scored 121.00 to upset Simpson Sith and climb to 2-6. Flint Tropics lost despite scoring 118.08, the third-highest total of the week. The Central standings remain separated, but three of its teams finished in the weekly top three.",
      "The standings continue to disagree with the underlying numbers. Redwood is 7-1 but ranks sixth in PF and fifth in all-play. California is 6-2 while ranking ninth in PF and ninth in all-play. Off Boys fell to 3-5 despite remaining third in PF and third in all-play. The difference between schedule outcomes and weekly strength is no longer a small-sample curiosity.",
      "Your Mom may be the hottest team outside the top tier. A 123.22 win over Eskimo Brothers gives Your Mom a 122.73-point average over the last three weeks, best in the league. The record is only 4-4, but that recent scoring surge has pulled the East into a three-team fight behind Sullco.",
      "THE Barton Spartans suffered the week’s harshest collapse. A 57.38-point rivalry loss to Space Cadets was the lowest score of Week 8 and the second-lowest team score recorded through eight completed weeks, behind only Medford MountainMen’s 58.08 in Week 4."
    ],
